Kiebitz is **source-available, not open source**. The source code is published
so that anyone can read it, audit it, and build it for their own private use.
It is not placed in the public domain and it does not carry an open-source
license: every right not expressly granted below is reserved by the copyright
holder.

1. Definitions
--------------

"Software" means the Kiebitz source code, build scripts, assets and
documentation contained in this repository, excluding the Third-Party
Components described in section 6.

"You" means the individual exercising the rights granted in section 2.

2. What you may do
------------------

Permission is granted, free of charge, to any individual to:

  a) view, read, study and privately modify the Software;
  b) compile and run the Software, including privately modified versions, on
     devices you own or personally control, for your own personal use;
  c) create and keep private copies and backups for the purposes above;
  d) quote short excerpts of the source code for the purpose of discussion,
     review, teaching, bug reports or academic citation, with attribution.

The permission to modify in 2(a) and to run modified versions in 2(b) does not
extend to removing, disabling, bypassing or reproducing the entitlement
verification, the feature gating of Kiebitz Plus, or the advertising surface of
the free version. Rights that mandatory law grants you regardless — in
particular Art. 5 and 6 of Directive 2009/24/EC and §§ 69d, 69e UrhG — remain
unaffected.

3. What you may not do
----------------------

Except as expressly permitted in section 2 or by mandatory applicable law, you
may not:

  a) distribute, publish, sublicense, lend, rent, sell or otherwise make
     available the Software or any derivative of it, in source or binary form,
     to any third party;
  b) publish or submit the Software, or any derivative or repackaged form of
     it, to any application store, package repository or other distribution
     channel;
  c) incorporate the Software, or any part of it, into a commercial product or
     service, or otherwise exploit the Software itself for commercial advantage
     or monetary compensation — for example by selling it, licensing it,
     bundling it, or offering it to others as a hosted or managed service;
  d) use the Software to create a product that substitutes for or competes with
     Kiebitz;
  e) remove, obscure or alter any copyright, license, attribution or
     third-party notice contained in the Software, including the files under
     `src-tauri/resources/stockfish/` and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`;
  f) use the name "Kiebitz", the Kiebitz logo or the Kiebitz visual identity to
     identify any product other than the original Software, or in a way that
     suggests endorsement.

Section 3(c) restricts what you may do *with the Software as such*. It does not
restrict what you do *with Kiebitz as a user*: running it while you teach, coach,
stream, compete or otherwise earn money from your own chess activity is
permitted, and is what the Kiebitz Plus subscription is sold for (see section 4).

Rights beyond this license — redistribution, commercial exploitation of the
Software itself, forking as a separate product — may be granted individually.
Ask via https://github.com/kiebitz-dev/Kiebitz/issues.

4. Official binaries and Kiebitz Plus
-------------------------------------

Binaries published by the copyright holder (GitHub releases, and any app store
listing) are made available for your own use under this same license. There is
no limit on the purpose for which you use them; section 3(c) applies to the
Software as source and derivatives, not to your use of an official build.

The free version of Kiebitz and the paid Kiebitz Plus subscription are governed
by the Terms of Service at https://kiebitz.dev/terms, which also carry the
subscription, payment, withdrawal and cancellation terms. Where those terms and
this license address the same question, those terms prevail for the official
binaries and for the subscription. Store-distributed builds are additionally
subject to the terms of the store that distributes them.

Nothing in this license restricts your rights under section 6 with regard to the
Third-Party Components bundled in those binaries.

5. Contributions
----------------

Contributions are welcome but not required. By submitting a contribution (for
example a pull request or a patch in an issue) you grant the copyright holder a
perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free, non-exclusive right to use,
modify, relicense and distribute that contribution as part of the Software,
including in commercially distributed versions. You confirm that you are
entitled to grant that right. You retain the copyright in your contribution.

6. Third-party components
-------------------------

The Software uses and, in its distributed builds, bundles third-party
components that are licensed by their respective authors under their own terms.
Those terms govern those components and are **not** superseded by this license.
In particular:

  - **Stockfish** (chess engine) is licensed under GPL-3.0. Kiebitz runs it as
    an unmodified separate process communicating over the UCI text protocol; no
    part of Stockfish is linked into Kiebitz. Notices, the full license text,
    the exact source commit, and a written offer for the corresponding source
    are in `src-tauri/resources/stockfish/` and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.
  - **Lichess puzzle database** — CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication).
  - **Piece sets, board graphics and fonts** bundled with the Software carry
    their own licenses and attribution requirements — CC BY-SA 3.0, Apache-2.0
    and OFL among them — and some of them apply to artwork that is only offered
    with Kiebitz Plus. The per-set attributions and the terms that go with them
    are in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.
  - Third-party libraries pulled in via npm and Cargo remain under their own
    licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC, BSD, OFL and others).

Where this license and a third-party license conflict for a given component,
the third-party license prevails for that component.

